menu "BlueAudio Puck: power"

    config PUCK_BT_TX_POWER_LEVEL
        int "Bluetooth transmit power level (0=-12dBm .. 7=+9dBm)"
        default 4
        range 0 7
        help
            Caps the radio's transmit power. The source is usually in the same
            pocket, so the top of the range spends current on range nobody is
            using. Raise it if the puck lives in a bag with the phone across
            the room. 4 is 0 dBm.

    config PUCK_CPU_MAX_FREQ_MHZ
        int "Maximum CPU frequency (MHz)"
        default 160
        range 80 240
        help
            SBC decode plus a handful of biquads fits comfortably at 160 MHz.
            240 buys headroom for more DSP at a noticeable current cost.

    config PUCK_CPU_MIN_FREQ_MHZ
        int "Minimum CPU frequency (MHz)"
        default 80
        range 10 240
        help
            Floor the CPU drops to when nothing needs the cycles. Only has an
            effect when frequency scaling is compiled in.

    config PUCK_IDLE_SLEEP_MINUTES
        int "Deep sleep after this many idle minutes (0 disables)"
        default 15
        range 0 240
        help
            Counts only while nothing is connected. A connected but paused
            source never triggers it -- a puck that vanishes from under a
            paused phone is worse than a flat one. This does not extend
            playback at all; it is what stops the puck going flat overnight in
            a bag.

endmenu
